        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nKey Features\n• Renovated 4-bedroom property on an elevated site on the popular Mountain Road, Cahir.\n• South-facing 1.16-acre site with mature gardens and open views of the surrounding picturesque countryside.\n• Secluded site with electronic gates offering unrivalled privacy.\n• Modern open-plan living accommodation offering panoramic views of the Knockmealdown and Comeragh mountain ranges.\n• Two spacious reception rooms with a connecting outdoor terrace offering ample space for outdoor-indoor entertaining.\n• Potential to provide further residential accommodation (subject to planning).\n• Directly adjacent to Scarragh Woods, offering trails for walking, cycling and horse riding.\n• Approx. 5-minute drive to the local town of Cahir (2.8km).\n• Convenient 5 minute-drive to the M8 motorway Dublin/Cork.\n \nOverview \nThe Villa is situated on an elevated south-facing site overlooking the town of Cahir and the surrounding picturesque countryside. The house itself offers generous open-plan living accommodation boasting vistas of the surrounding Knockmealdown and Comeragh mountain ranges. The property is located very close to the town of Cahir on the popular Mountain Road, while sitting comfortably in the countryside providing the best of both worlds. The property is located directly adjacent to Scarragh Woods, offering trails for walking, cycling and horse riding while offering unrivalled privacy guarded by electronic gates.\n \nThe house has been fully refurbished in 2025/2026 and is presented in turn-key condition with no extra expense needed. The recent refurbishment has included solar panels (including battery storage system), electric gates, EV charging, insulation upgrades, new kitchen and upgraded bathrooms. The living accommodation features two spacious reception rooms with a connecting outdoor terrace and rear courtyard offering ample space for outdoor-indoor entertaining. The property provides four well-proportioned bedrooms, a family bathroom, Master en-suite bathroom and separate WC connected to the main living accommodation. The house is set on a large 1.16-acre site with several outbuildings and offers potential to provide further residential accommodation (subject to planning).\n \nCahir town is ideally located on the crossroads of the M8 Dublin/Cork motorway and the Limerick/Waterford route giving commuters an ideal base. Cahir is a thriving market town with a large tourist industry built around the Galtee mountains and the iconic Cahir castle giving rise to many coffee shops, restaurants and pubs. The town has developed as a centre for outdoor pursuits due to its ideal location at the foot of the Galtee mountains and sitting along the river Suir. The town provides a multitude of outdoor pursuits for all ages and abilities including mountain walks, horse-riding, river walks along by Cahir castle and the Swiss Cottage and water sports along the ever-developing 53km 'Blue Way'.\n \nCahir town itself offers much in the way of employment but additionally a short 20-minute drive to Clonmel opens up a wealth of job opportunities in Pharmaceutical, Engineering, to name but a few. The town is well-served with all amenities needed in modern life including a range of schools, medical, sports facilities with many sports and social clubs and leisure pursuits all on offer.\n \nThe Villa is a property with much to offer. Viewing is highly advised.\n \n Connections\n \n• Cahir (2.8km) approx. 5-minute drive\n• M8 motorway (to Dublin/Cork) - 5 minute-drive\n• Cashel (20km) approx. 15-minute drive\n• Clonmel (20km) approx. 20-minute drive\n• Thurles Train Station (to Dublin/Cork) (39km) approx. 30-minute drive\n• Cork Airport (85km) approx. 1 hours' drive\n• Cork city (80km) approx. 1 hours' drive\n• Limerick city (65km) approx.1 hours' drive"
      },
